# Line endings. Text is stored and checked out as LF everywhere, whatever
# `core.autocrlf` says on the machine. Until 2026-11-25 the repo had neither
# this file nor a rule: 86 of its 723 text files were CRLF, a one-line edit
# with the wrong tool rewrote a whole file, and the diff said nothing useful.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts keep CRLF in the working tree.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Never touched, whatever git guesses.
*.wav binary
*.mp3 binary
*.ogg binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.apk binary
*.keystore binary
*.sf2 binary
*.mid binary
*.lnk binary

# Puncheoke — the instrument — is forked to its own product and its code here
# is not ours to rework. These paths are left byte-for-byte as committed
# (some CRLF, some LF) so they stay diffable against the fork. The same list
# is in .prettierignore; keep the two in step.
docs/puncheoke/** -text
src/app/(tabs)/puncheokie/** -text
src/domain/instrument/** -text
src/instrument/** -text
tools/punchbridge/** -text
tools/tablet-voice/** -text
*[Ii]nstrument* -text
